   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Directionals 来 and 去",
     "texto": [
      "**来** points movement towards the speaker and **去** moves it away from the speaker. In expressions such as **进来** («come in, towards here») and **出去** («go out, away from here»), the directional verb goes after the main verb.",
      "Context decides the reference point: **拿进来** is to bring something inwards, while **拿出去** is to take it outwards."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
